research/audit/wave4-foundations.provenance.jsonl:16:{"id": "def-cofinality", "statement": "ai-altered", "proof": "not-applicable", "evidence": "semantic-source", "urls": ["https://www.homepages.ucl.ac.uk/~ucahcjm/ast/ast_notes_4.pdf"], "rationale": "The sourced definition is the least length of a cofinal map. The item uses it for all ordinals, not only limits, and folds regular/singular terminology and the explicit choice-free convention into the definition. At A4 the model-side fetch resolved the UCL PDF with HTTP 200 and exposed the cited mathematical text. A6 URL disposition (Alpha, 2026-08-04): the recorded www.ucl.ac.uk path returns HTTP 404; the same notes are live at www.homepages.ucl.ac.uk, fetched at HTTP 200 and confirmed to be Chapter 4, Cardinal Arithmetic, whose section 4.4 defines cofinality, regular and singular cardinals and computes cf(aleph_omega) = omega. The URL was rewritten in the item and here; the source itself is unchanged.", "alpha_concurred": false, "at": "2026-08-04"}
research/audit/wave4-foundations.provenance.jsonl:17:{"id": "thm-cofinality-basics", "statement": "ai-altered", "proof": "ai-altered", "evidence": "semantic-source", "urls": ["https://www.homepages.ucl.ac.uk/~ucahcjm/ast/ast_notes_4.pdf"], "rationale": "The sources give cf(0), successor cofinality, infinite-limit cofinality, regularity of cofinalities, and minimum cofinal-set size. The item bundles those results and adapts the proofs to its all-ordinal definition. At A4 the model-side fetch resolved the UCL PDF with HTTP 200 and exposed the cited mathematical text. A6 URL disposition (Alpha, 2026-08-04): the recorded www.ucl.ac.uk path returns HTTP 404; the same notes are live at www.homepages.ucl.ac.uk, fetched at HTTP 200 and confirmed to be Chapter 4, Cardinal Arithmetic, whose section 4.4 defines cofinality, regular and singular cardinals and computes cf(aleph_omega) = omega. The URL was rewritten in the item and here; the source itself is unchanged.", "alpha_concurred": false, "at": "2026-08-04"}
research/audit/wave4-foundations.provenance.jsonl:18:{"id": "thm-regularity-of-the-alephs", "statement": "ai-altered", "proof": "ai-altered", "evidence": "semantic-source", "urls": ["https://www.homepages.ucl.ac.uk/~ucahcjm/ast/ast_notes_4.pdf"], "rationale": "The literature gives regularity of omega and successor cardinals under choice and singularity of aleph_omega. The item bundles four clauses, isolates the exact AC expenditure, and adds the least-singular conclusion. At A4 the model-side fetch resolved the UCL PDF with HTTP 200 and exposed the cited mathematical text. A6 URL disposition (Alpha, 2026-08-04): the recorded www.ucl.ac.uk path returns HTTP 404; the same notes are live at www.homepages.ucl.ac.uk, fetched at HTTP 200 and confirmed to be Chapter 4, Cardinal Arithmetic, whose section 4.4 defines cofinality, regular and singular cardinals and computes cf(aleph_omega) = omega. The URL was rewritten in the item and here; the source itself is unchanged.", "alpha_concurred": false, "at": "2026-08-04"}
research/audit/wave4-foundations.provenance.jsonl:21:{"id": "cor-cofinality-of-a-cardinal-power", "statement": "ai-altered", "proof": "ai-altered", "evidence": "semantic-source", "urls": ["https://math.colorado.edu/~kearnes/Teaching/Courses/F25/cardinals_arithmetic.pdf"], "rationale": "The sources prove kappa<kappa^cf(kappa) and cf(2^kappa)>kappa. The item combines those results with the continuum specialization and derives them through its family-form König theorem. At A4 the model-side fetch resolved the Colorado PDF with HTTP 200 and exposed the cited mathematical text.", "alpha_concurred": false, "at": "2026-08-04"}
research/audit/wave4-foundations.provenance.jsonl:24:{"id": "fs-every-aleph-is-regular", "statement": "ai-altered", "proof": "ai-altered", "evidence": "semantic-source", "urls": ["https://www.homepages.ucl.ac.uk/~ucahcjm/ast/ast_notes_4.pdf"], "rationale": "The sources state regularity of successor cardinals under choice and singularity of aleph_omega with countable cofinality. The item reframes that standard boundary as the false universal claim that every aleph is regular. At A4 the model-side fetch resolved the UCL PDF with HTTP 200 and exposed the cited mathematical text. A6 URL disposition (Alpha, 2026-08-04): the recorded www.ucl.ac.uk path returns HTTP 404; the same notes are live at www.homepages.ucl.ac.uk, fetched at HTTP 200 and confirmed to be Chapter 4, Cardinal Arithmetic, whose section 4.4 defines cofinality, regular and singular cardinals and computes cf(aleph_omega) = omega. The URL was rewritten in the item and here; the source itself is unchanged.", "alpha_concurred": false, "at": "2026-08-04"}
research/audit/wave4-foundations.provenance.jsonl:25:{"id": "fs-cardinal-exponentiation-is-strictly-monotone-in-the-base", "statement": "ai-altered", "proof": "ai-altered", "evidence": "semantic-source", "urls": ["https://people.math.harvard.edu/~wboney/fall16/settheory.pdf"], "rationale": "The sources give the exponent-collapse law 2<=kappa<=lambda with lambda infinite implies kappa^lambda=2^lambda, which yields the displayed aleph_0/aleph_1 witness. The item reframes it as failure of a false strict base-monotonicity claim. At A4 the model-side fetch resolved the Harvard PDF with HTTP 200 and exposed the cited mathematical text.", "alpha_concurred": false, "at": "2026-08-04"}
