research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-refuter-refute-f4-cofinality.log:6746:    57	[L3] $\operatorname{cf}(\alpha)$ is the least length of a cofinal map into $\alpha$, a strictly increasing witness of that length exists, and for a limit ordinal $\lambda$ the value $\operatorname{cf}(\lambda)$ is an infinite cardinal with $\operatorname{cf}(\lambda) \le \lambda$ ([[def-cofinality]], [[lem-cofinality-is-well-defined]], [[thm-cofinality-basics]], [[def-cofinal-subset-of-an-ordinal]]).
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-refuter-refute-f4-cofinality.log:6778:    89	**What clause (b) rules out, concretely.** If $2^{\aleph_0}$ were $\aleph_\omega$ then its cofinality would be $\aleph_0$ by [[thm-regularity-of-the-alephs]], contradicting clause (c); that refutation is carried out in [[fs-the-continuum-has-cardinality-aleph-omega]]. The same test applies to any proposed value whose cofinality can be computed. Clause (c) is a restriction and not a determination: it excludes values and selects none.
