research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-refuter-refute-f4-cofinality.result.json:16:  "tail": "\nEVIDENCE: The Statement begins verbatim: \"**Assume the Axiom of Choice** ([[def-axiom-of-choice]]). Let $\\kappa$ be an infinite cardinal.\" `def-cardinal-arithmetic` further states that exponentiation is defined exactly when the function set is well-orderable and is universally available under the Axiom of Choice.\n\nSEVERITY: fatal\n\nMINIMAL REPAIR: Prefix the existing title with \"Assuming the Axiom of Choice, \".\n\n### FINDING 7 — cor-cofinality-of-a-cardinal-power — L7 cites no target defining infinite cardinals\n\nLOCATION: Facts & Assumptions, line 65\n\nQUOTE: \"[L7] Every infinite cardinal is a limit ordinal, and a cardinal is infinite exactly when $\\omega \\le \\kappa$ ([[thm-cardinal-arithmetic-agrees-with-finite-counting]], [[def-limit-ordinal]]).\"\n\nDEFECT: The cited theorem supports only the first clause, while the cited definition explains limit ordinals. Neither states the second equivalence.\n\nEVIDENCE: `thm-cardinal-arithmetic-agrees-with-finite-counting` states: \"**(b)** Every infinite cardinal is a limit ordinal.\" The equivalence appears in the uncited declared dependency `def-cardinal-arithmetic`: \"A cardinal $\\kappa$ is ... infinite when $\\omega \\subseteq \\kappa$, that is $\\omega \\le \\kappa$.\"\n\nSEVERITY: fatal\n\nMINIMAL REPAIR: Add `[[def-cardinal-arithmetic]]` to L7 as the citation for the second clause.\n\n### FINDING 8 — cor-cofinality-of-a-cardinal-power — L10 overstates the ordinal-union lemma\n\nLOCATION: Facts & Assumptions, line 71\n\nQUOTE: \"[L10] Ordinals satisfy trichotomy, $\\alpha \\subseteq \\beta$ iff $\\alpha \\in \\beta$ or $\\alpha = \\beta$, the union of a set of ordinals is its least upper bound, and every nonempty set of ordinals has an $\\in$-least element; a function is injective when equality of two values forces equality of the corresponding inputs ([[lem-ordinal-trichotomy]], [[lem-ordinal-basics]], [[def-well-order]], [[def-injection-surjection-bijection]]).\"\n\nDEFECT: `lem-ordinal-basics` states only that the union is an ordinal. No cited target states the least-upper-bound clause, which is unnecessary for this proof.\n\nEVIDENCE: The cited target's complete union clause is: \"**(e)** if $A$ is any set of ordinals then $\\bigcup A$ is an ordinal.\"\n\nSEVERITY: fatal\n\nMINIMAL REPAIR: Delete \"the union of a set of ordinals is its least upper bound, and\" from L10.\n\n## Coverage\nItems read in full: def-cofinality, lem-cofinality-is-well-defined, thm-cofinality-basics, thm-regularity-of-the-alephs, def-infinite-cardinal-sum-and-product, thm-konig, cor-cofinality-of-a-cardinal-power\nItems not read, and why: none\nFacts checked against their target on disk: 40\nFindings: 8 fatal, 0 nonfatal"
