research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations-apply.log:5943:    17	{"id":"thm-cofinality-basics","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://math.ucla.edu/~marks/notes/set_theory_notes.pdf","https://people.math.harvard.edu/~wboney/fall16/settheory.pdf"],"rationale":"The sources give cf(0), successor cofinality, infinite-limit cofinality, regularity of cofinalities, and minimum cofinal-set size. The item bundles those results and adapts the proofs to its all-ordinal definition. Every listed URL was opened through the model-side web fetch route and returned rendered HTML or PDF content (HTTP 200).","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-04"}
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations-apply.log:5944:    18	{"id":"thm-regularity-of-the-alephs","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://math.ucla.edu/~marks/notes/set_theory_notes.pdf","https://people.math.harvard.edu/~wboney/fall16/settheory.pdf"],"rationale":"The literature gives regularity of omega and successor cardinals under choice and singularity of aleph_omega. The item bundles four clauses, isolates the exact AC expenditure, and adds the least-singular conclusion. Every listed URL was opened through the model-side web fetch route and returned rendered HTML or PDF content (HTTP 200).","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-04"}
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations-apply.log:5947:    21	{"id":"cor-cofinality-of-a-cardinal-power","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://math.colorado.edu/~kearnes/Teaching/Courses/F25/cardinals_arithmetic.pdf","https://math.ucla.edu/~marks/notes/set_theory_notes.pdf"],"rationale":"The sources prove kappa<kappa^cf(kappa) and cf(2^kappa)>kappa. The item combines those results with the continuum specialization and derives them through its family-form König theorem. Every listed URL was opened through the model-side web fetch route and returned rendered HTML or PDF content (HTTP 200).","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-04"}
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations-apply.log:5950:    24	{"id":"fs-every-aleph-is-regular","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://people.math.harvard.edu/~wboney/fall16/settheory.pdf","https://math.ucla.edu/~marks/notes/set_theory_notes.pdf"],"rationale":"The sources state regularity of successor cardinals under choice and singularity of aleph_omega with countable cofinality. The item reframes that standard boundary as the false universal claim that every aleph is regular. Every listed URL was opened through the model-side web fetch route and returned rendered HTML or PDF content (HTTP 200).","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-04"}
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations-apply.log:5951:    25	{"id":"fs-cardinal-exponentiation-is-strictly-monotone-in-the-base","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://people.math.harvard.edu/~wboney/fall16/settheory.pdf","https://math.colorado.edu/~kearnes/Teaching/Courses/F25/cardinals_arithmetic.pdf"],"rationale":"The sources give the exponent-collapse law 2<=kappa<=lambda with lambda infinite implies kappa^lambda=2^lambda, which yields the displayed aleph_0/aleph_1 witness. The item reframes it as failure of a false strict base-monotonicity claim. Every listed URL was opened through the model-side web fetch route and returned rendered HTML or PDF content (HTTP 200).","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-04"}
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations-apply.log:6448:**What it is used for on this page.** With $\lambda_i$ constant the product becomes an exponential, and the resulting inequality bounds the cofinality of a power from below; that consequence is [[cor-cofinality-of-a-cardinal-power]], and it is the only ZFC constraint on $2^{\aleph_0}$ established here.
