research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log:539129:+ ['def-cofinality','ai-altered','not-applicable','semantic-source',[M,K],'The sourced definition is the least length of a cofinal map. The item uses it for all ordinals, not only limits, and folds regular/singular terminology and the explicit choice-free convention into the definition.'],
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log:539130:+ ['thm-cofinality-basics','ai-altered','ai-altered','semantic-source',[M,K],'The sources give cf(0), successor cofinality, infinite-limit cofinality, regularity of cofinalities, and minimum cofinal-set size. The item bundles those results and adapts the proofs to its all-ordinal definition.'],
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log:539131:+ ['thm-regularity-of-the-alephs','ai-altered','ai-altered','semantic-source',[M,K],'The literature gives regularity of omega and successor cardinals under choice and singularity of aleph_omega. The item bundles four clauses, isolates the exact AC expenditure, and adds the least-singular conclusion.'],
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log:539134:+ ['cor-cofinality-of-a-cardinal-power','ai-altered','ai-altered','semantic-source',[C,M],'The sources prove kappa<kappa^cf(kappa) and cf(2^kappa)>kappa. The item combines those results with the continuum specialization and derives them through its family-form König theorem.'],
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log:539137:+ ['fs-every-aleph-is-regular','ai-generated','ai-generated','none',[],'This is positively a fabricated universal overgeneralization from omega and successor alephs. Its truth risk is discharged by the standard explicit counterexample cf(aleph_omega)=aleph_0<aleph_omega.'],
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log:539138:+ ['fs-cardinal-exponentiation-is-strictly-monotone-in-the-base','ai-generated','ai-generated','none',[],'This is positively a fabricated strengthening of weak base monotonicity. Its truth risk is discharged by the displayed ZFC witness aleph_0<aleph_1 but aleph_0^aleph_0=aleph_1^aleph_0=2^aleph_0.'],
