research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log:539367:+{"id":"def-cofinality","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"not-applicable","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://math.ucla.edu/~marks/notes/set_theory_notes.pdf","https://people.math.harvard.edu/~wboney/fall16/settheory.pdf"],"rationale":"The sourced definition is the least length of a cofinal map. The item uses it for all ordinals, not only limits, and folds regular/singular terminology and the explicit choice-free convention into the definition. Every listed URL was opened through the model-side web fetch route and returned rendered HTML or PDF content (HTTP 200).","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-04"}
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log:539368:+{"id":"thm-cofinality-basics","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://math.ucla.edu/~marks/notes/set_theory_notes.pdf","https://people.math.harvard.edu/~wboney/fall16/settheory.pdf"],"rationale":"The sources give cf(0), successor cofinality, infinite-limit cofinality, regularity of cofinalities, and minimum cofinal-set size. The item bundles those results and adapts the proofs to its all-ordinal definition. Every listed URL was opened through the model-side web fetch route and returned rendered HTML or PDF content (HTTP 200).","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-04"}
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log:539369:+{"id":"thm-regularity-of-the-alephs","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://math.ucla.edu/~marks/notes/set_theory_notes.pdf","https://people.math.harvard.edu/~wboney/fall16/settheory.pdf"],"rationale":"The literature gives regularity of omega and successor cardinals under choice and singularity of aleph_omega. The item bundles four clauses, isolates the exact AC expenditure, and adds the least-singular conclusion. Every listed URL was opened through the model-side web fetch route and returned rendered HTML or PDF content (HTTP 200).","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-04"}
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log:539372:+{"id":"cor-cofinality-of-a-cardinal-power","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://math.colorado.edu/~kearnes/Teaching/Courses/F25/cardinals_arithmetic.pdf","https://math.ucla.edu/~marks/notes/set_theory_notes.pdf"],"rationale":"The sources prove kappa<kappa^cf(kappa) and cf(2^kappa)>kappa. The item combines those results with the continuum specialization and derives them through its family-form König theorem. Every listed URL was opened through the model-side web fetch route and returned rendered HTML or PDF content (HTTP 200).","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-04"}
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log:539375:+{"id":"fs-every-aleph-is-regular","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://people.math.harvard.edu/~wboney/fall16/settheory.pdf","https://math.ucla.edu/~marks/notes/set_theory_notes.pdf"],"rationale":"The sources state regularity of successor cardinals under choice and singularity of aleph_omega with countable cofinality. The item reframes that standard boundary as the false universal claim that every aleph is regular. Every listed URL was opened through the model-side web fetch route and returned rendered HTML or PDF content (HTTP 200).","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-04"}
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-foundations.log:539376:+{"id":"fs-cardinal-exponentiation-is-strictly-monotone-in-the-base","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://people.math.harvard.edu/~wboney/fall16/settheory.pdf","https://math.colorado.edu/~kearnes/Teaching/Courses/F25/cardinals_arithmetic.pdf"],"rationale":"The sources give the exponent-collapse law 2<=kappa<=lambda with lambda infinite implies kappa^lambda=2^lambda, which yields the displayed aleph_0/aleph_1 witness. The item reframes it as failure of a false strict base-monotonicity claim. Every listed URL was opened through the model-side web fetch route and returned rendered HTML or PDF content (HTTP 200).","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-04"}
